inst/extdata/*_interactions_v1.rds are correction maps generated for SpaMTPdb.
They contain row indices and interaction labels, not pathway graphs. They
apply only to collections whose SHA-256 fingerprint matches. Source graphs
retain their database-specific terms, including KEGG, Reactome, WikiPathways
and SMPDB; SpaMTPdb's MIT code licence does not relicense those databases.
The accompanying inst/manifest/pathway_interactions_provenance.csv identifies
the source URLs and checksums. See help("spaMTPdbResource") and the
source-repository recipe data-raw/rebuild_pathway_interactions.R.

AI-assisted development

OpenAI Codex assisted with pathway-interaction correction transfer, regression
tests and Bioconductor review updates. Git history records the scope of the
changes. Maintainers remain responsible for reviewing the contribution, its
reliability and its maintenance. AI tools are not listed as package authors.

